# Who has to review a change before it merges.
#
# This file is only enforced if branch protection on main requires review from
# code owners. Without that setting it is documentation, not a control.
#
# Both accounts below hold admin on the repository, so the ownership is the
# same everywhere today. The paths are listed separately anyway: they are the
# ones where a merged change alters what runs or what the examples teach, and
# they should stay explicit if ownership is ever narrowed.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so the specific rules below take
# precedence over the catch-all.

*                        @AminaEmenena @Dr-Cyber-OG

# Runs with this repository's token.
/.github/workflows/      @AminaEmenena @Dr-Cyber-OG
/.github/dependabot.yml  @AminaEmenena @Dr-Cyber-OG

# The scripts the README tells other people to run against their own repos.
/tools/                  @AminaEmenena @Dr-Cyber-OG

# The teaching material. The all-zero SHAs in the after.yml files are
# deliberate and a real one must never be committed here.
/examples/               @AminaEmenena @Dr-Cyber-OG

# The deliberately unsafe fixture. It is inert only while it stays out of the
# repository root, where GitHub would execute it.
/demo/                   @AminaEmenena @Dr-Cyber-OG

# The checks that enforce everything above.
/tests/                  @AminaEmenena @Dr-Cyber-OG

# This file.
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @AminaEmenena @Dr-Cyber-OG
